::PC_U05_L07_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L07_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.8
Question:
Which idea is correct about hyperbolas?
{
~A. A hyperbola has one circular radius.#This choice misses the key structure of the representation or conic. Identify the definition, equation form, and key features before choosing an answer.
=B. A hyperbola has two branches and asymptotes that guide its graph.#Correct. Hyperbolas have two branches and asymptotes that help shape the graph.
~C. A hyperbola always opens upward only.#This choice misses the key structure of the representation or conic. Identify the definition, equation form, and key features before choosing an answer.
~D. The center is never used.#This choice misses the key structure of the representation or conic. Identify the definition, equation form, and key features before choosing an answer.
}
